    "linkType": "mapsCity",
    "blurb": "Washington's wing scene refuses to pick a single style, and that is its strength. The city treats the wing as a blank canvas, layering global technique over home flavors like sweet-tangy mumbo sauce and Old Bay. Chase shatteringly crisp Korean fried wings at KoChix and Bonchon, smoke-kissed barbecue versions at DCity Smokehouse and Federalist Pig, cumin-glazed Cambodian wings at Maketto, halal za'atar wings in Adams Morgan, soul food platters on U Street, and legit Buffalo wings besides. From dollar-wing happy hours to chef-driven counters, the District rewards anyone willing to explore.",
