    "linkType": "mapsCity",
    "blurb": "Manhattan runs on coffee, and its best cups come from a deep bench of specialty roasters and design-forward cafes scattered from the East Village to Midtown. La Cabra brings Nordic light roasts and cardamom buns to Second Avenue, Devocion rushes farm-fresh Colombian beans to its skylit Flatiron room, and longtime favorites like Abraco and Culture Espresso pull some of the city's most precise espresso. Whether you want a counter-service cortado, a maximalist latte under a copper dome at Felix, or a quiet pour-over at Hi-Collar, this list covers the genuinely great places to drink coffee in the borough.",
